NEARS-2448 — live QA session summary (device emulator-5558, AVD NEARS_2411_QA)
================================================================================

Device: reclaimed a fresh/residue-only Android emulator (emulator-5558) after
the full 7-device pool was saturated by other live sessions for a bounded
~10min wait; disk precheck passed (3.4GB free). Booted UserApp fresh
(`flutter run -d emulator-5558 --debug`, ~296s assembleDebug under heavy
shared-host contention from ~6 concurrent worktree builds), then survived one
mid-session drop (`am force-stop` during a zone switch) via
`scripts/qa-reconnect.sh UserApp emulator-5558` (state-preserving flutter
attach, no reinstall, login/cart intact).

Navigation constraint found + worked around: CampaignScreen is NOT reachable
via any currently-seeded module's Home screen — `MiddleSectionBannerView`
(the campaign carousel) is mounted ONLY in `ShopHomeScreen`
(`isShop` == module_type `ecommerce`), and no ecommerce/"Shop" module is
seeded in this fork (Grocery/Food/Pharmacy/Parcel only, confirmed via
`GroceryHomeScreen`/`FoodHomeScreen` source — neither includes
`MiddleSectionBannerView`). OS-level deep linking is also disabled
(`flutter_deeplinking_enabled=false` in AndroidManifest.xml). Reached the
screen instead via a direct Dart VM Service `evaluate` call
(`Get.toNamed("/basic-campaign?module=1&data=<base64 BasicCampaignModel>")`,
the exact route+payload shape `RouteHelper.getBasicCampaignRoute()` builds) —
a read-only runtime debug action, no product code touched. Flagging the
unreachable-via-UI finding as a followup (drift from the QA Test Scope's
suggested "tap a campaign banner" path), not a task_bug (out of this
ticket's 2-file scope).

Zone: switched from the default zone 2 (Abu Dhabi) to zone 1 (Dhaka demo
zone) via `adb emu geo fix` to store 1's exact coordinates + "Use my current
location" on the map picker, to get a real ACTIVE store (id 1, "Nears Mart")
for full-fidelity success-state evidence (campaign 1 has a 2nd store, id 21
in zone 2, but it is status=0/inactive so zone 2 alone would only ever show
the empty-store branch).

Seed data used (verified via read-only DB SELECT, Admin/multi_food_db):
  campaign 1 "QA Single-Store Campaign A" — 1 active participating store
    (Nears Mart, zone 1) -> success/non-empty state.
  campaign 2 "QA Single-Store Campaign B" — 0 participating stores (no
    campaign_store row at all) -> genuine empty-state fixture, any zone.

Per-AC live results (all on emulator-5558, package com.izzes.nears pid 6148):

AC1 [ui] failed fetch -> full-pane NErrorRetry:
  - Transport failure (wifi+data disabled via `adb shell svc wifi/data
    disable`, i.e. airplane-mode-equivalent): `[FAIL] endpoint=/api/v1/
    campaigns/basic-campaign-details http_status=null type=ApiFailure
    transport_error=socket msg="api request threw" correlation_id=...` ->
    UI renders "Something went wrong" / "Please try again" / "Retry" full
    pane. PASS. Screenshot: ac1-transport-failure-NErrorRetry.png
  - Invalid/non-resolving campaign id (id=99999): CONFIRMS the finding
    flagged in the prior BLOCKED pass as a live TypeError, not just a static
    trace (see bug-invalid-campaign-id-CONFIRMED-LIVE.log/.png below) — the
    screen does NOT render NErrorRetry for this trigger, it stays
    permanently blank (only "Back" in the a11y tree). This is a genuine
    AC1 gap for this specific documented repro method.

AC2 [behav] Retry re-calls + recovers:
  - From the transport-failure error state, tapped "Retry" (network
    re-enabled first) -> `[NET] endpoint=/api/v1/campaigns/
    basic-campaign-details http_status=200` -> screen recovers to the full
    loaded state (header card "QA Single-Store Campaign A" + "Nears Mart"
    store card). PASS. Screenshot: ac2-retry-recovers-to-loaded-state.png
  - Busy-latch / no-double-fire: NOT independently re-derived via rapid taps
    this pass (network round-trip timing on a shared/contended host makes a
    deterministic double-tap race hard to stage via discrete adb taps) —
    relying on (a) static confirmation that CampaignScreen's onRetry returns
    Future<void> (satisfies NErrorRetry's busy-latch precondition,
    packages/nears_dls/lib/components/nerrorretry/n_error_retry.dart
    _handleRetry()), and (b) that latch is a already-tested, reused DLS
    primitive (packages/nears_dls/test/components/n_error_retry_test.dart),
    not new code from this ticket. Single-tap recovery IS live-confirmed
    above.

AC3 [behav] loading state unchanged, no premature error flash:
  - Could not capture the live transient loading frame externally — the
    local dev backend resolves basic-campaign-details in well under the
    round-trip time of a second adb/VM-service call (observed ~550-760ms
    fetch, and two separate follow-up dumps both already showed the
    resolved state). This is a tooling/timing constraint, not a defect.
  - Verified instead via the CODE-LEVEL guarantee (deterministic, not
    probabilistic): CampaignController.getBasicCampaignDetails() sets
    `_hasError = false` SYNCHRONOUSLY, before the first `await` — so
    `hasError` can never read `true` during the in-flight window by
    construction, for either the initial mount OR a retry. During that
    window `basicCampaign` is also null, so CampaignScreen takes the
    non-error branch and ItemsView(stores: null) renders exactly the
    pre-existing shimmer (unchanged). Corroborated by the passing automated
    widget-test suite (4/4, see automated backstop).

AC4 [behav] empty-store success state unchanged, no error pane:
  - campaign 2 (0 stores, any zone) -> header card "QA Single-Store
    Campaign B" + "Stores" section + "No store available" (NoDataScreen,
    NEmptyState WITHOUT a retry action) — NOT NErrorRetry. hasError stays
    false since basicCampaign resolved non-null. PASS. Screenshot:
    ac4-empty-state-not-error.png

Regression sweep (bounded, UserApp-only, 2 logic files):
  - Store-list navigation: tapped "Nears Mart" from the loaded campaign
    screen -> navigated cleanly to the store's item grid (Mango/Cola/Rice
    visible), no errors. Clean.
  - RTL/Arabic: `Get.updateLocale(Locale('ar','SA'))` (live VM-service call,
